<p>This doesn't really do anything for me. Despite the themes of mystery inherent to the narrative, I never found myself searching for character motives or questioning Clouzot's actions. Everything he does lacks subtlety.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>So much for a dead-end career — I'll be able to leverage this hard. Promotions, advancement, it's all opening up now for me.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The character depth here is unsatisfyingly shallow. The mystery of 5041 itself isn't much better in places; it's missing that element of &quot;being personal&quot;, of having some real hook beyond the initial oddity of an object collected from a predecessor organization.</p>
<p>I also find it hard to believe the effects of the anomaly could somehow kill a village. That needs a better explanation.</p>

