			<div class="content" id="post-content-4653437">
									

<p>Is the &quot;SCC&quot; abbreviation used anywhere else? I've never seen it before and it kinda stands out as unusual.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The only room into which containment staff are allowed to enter is the antechamber, and only to deliver food or other provisions to SCP-5041</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The second half of this isn't a complete sentence, so the comma before &quot;and&quot; isn't correct.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Under no circumstances should the interior of SCC-01 be looked into.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The tone of this seems a bit iffy. What are the procedures if someone does do this? Even if its reason isn't known to staff, I doubt they would let it remain so imprecise.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Entertainment media given to SCP-5041 should not contain depictions of or references to any individuals or characters, real or fictional.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What sort of entertainment media doesn't have any characters? It seems fairly restrictive; even music without lyrics can &quot;refer to&quot; an individual by its history. Perhaps stating here what entertainment media is allowed would be more appropriate. The Foundation errs on the side of caution with these things.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The prisoner is to be allowed the materials with which to write and paint.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why didn't this make it to containment procedures?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There is no way to touch me that does cut you to shreds.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should that be &quot;doesn't&quot;?</p>
<p>This needs elaboration or redaction, especially the bit about &quot;otherwise cease to exist&quot;.</p>
<p>There's no link back to the original page once you're on the updated one.</p>
<p>Why does the main link take me to an out-of-date entry?</p>
<p>How did he kill a whole town with these powers, yet a single guy having diabetes killed him?</p>
<p>I really like the whole concept. There are a lot of articles where Foundation personnel are rewarded for jacking with stuff and encouraged to do research on subjects, but that's not what they're about. This is: using a containment procedure that makes no sense, without knowing why, because it works. It's a great story and I can tell there was a ton of work put into it. It just suffers from some tone issues; I tried pointing out where, but I'm having a hard time putting my finger on it exactly.</p>
</div>
</div>
