<p>I did like the anomaly itself, but the way the discovery is presented didn't do it for me. I can't pin-point the specifics as to why, but as mentioned above, Clouzot's character might have something to do with it. Felt less like I was trying to learn about the ability alongside the character, and more like I was just waiting and soaking in the info, if that makes sense.</p>
<p>I also don't understand why he got punished by the Ethics Committee. He was given the assignment and didn't break any rules, just used archived information to get a better idea on the anomaly, which is standard Foundation MO. Why would you assign someone to an SCP and then tell them off for doing their job? The death of the SCP was also not his fault (practically speaking) since there was almost no information about its abilities and no way to know this would happen. Considering the nature of the Foundation's work, an anomaly dying because of complete lack of knowledge, and no malicious intent or mala praxis, is one of those things that would happen eventually.</p>
<p>It's gonna be a -1 from me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
